{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition","kind":"proposition","title":"Hopf-link symmetric decomposition: $\\sigma_1^2 = q^2 e_+ + q^{-2} e_-$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-van-der-waals-hopf-channel","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-trm-hopf-sigma1-sq-closed-form"],"tags":["van-der-waals","hopf-link","wedderburn-decomposition","symmetric-block","hecke"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.HopfSymmetric.hopf_symmetric_decomposition","text":"hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition.md","leanSource":"hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition\"></a><p><em>The Hopf element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1^2</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_2(q)</code> formally weights the two blocks by their squared eigenvalues:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\sigma_1^2 = q^2 e_+ + q^{-2} e_-.</code></pre>\n<p><em>Equivalently, cleared of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2]_q = q+q^{-1}</code> denominator:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  [2]_q \\sigma_1^2 = q^2 (\\sigma_1+q^{-1}) + q^{-2} (q-\\sigma_1).</code></pre>\n<p><em>This formally derives from the Hecke relation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1^2 = (q-q^{-1})\\sigma_1 + 1</code>.</em></p>\n<p>Its value at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code> and the van der Waals reading are recorded in <a href=\"#rem:hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition-van-der-waals-reading\" data-at=\"information-theory/phase-transitions\">this remark</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"22.10.8","page":"b/prop-hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition","qa":{"counts":{"pass":88,"fail":3,"warn":1,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":78},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.HopfSymmetric.hopf_symmetric_decomposition","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/hopf-link-symmetric-decomposition.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
